        "is_last_child": false
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Pursuant to 49 United States Code § 60118, the Pipeline and Hazardous Materials Safety Administration (PHMSA) proposes to issue to Grayson a Compliance Order incorporating the following remedial requirements to ensure the compliance of Grayson with the pipeline safety regulations:",
      "text_span": "",
      "size": 9.0,
      "bold": 0,
      "font": "unknown",
      "all_cap": 0,
      "num_st": 0,
      "is_center": 0,
      "is_underline": 0,
      "label": "text",
      "page_no": 3,
      "structure": {
        "level": "Body",
        "level_index": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "path_text": "",
        "depth": 1,
        "h1_index_norm": 0,
        "sibling_index_norm": 0.9032258064516129,
        "is_first_child": false,
        "is_last_child": false
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In regard to Item number 1 of the Notice pertaining to the Williams Booster Station Breakout tanks, Grayson must install cathodic protection on the tanks at the William Booster Station within 180 days of receipt of the Final Order.",
      "text_span": "",
      "size": 9.0,
      "bold": 0,
      "font": "unknown",
      "all_cap": 0,
      "num_st": 0,
      "is_center": 0,
      "is_underline": 0,
      "label": "list_item",
      "page_no": 3,
      "structure": {
        "level": "Body",
        "level_index": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "path_text": "",
        "depth": 1,
        "h1_index_norm": 0,
        "sibling_index_norm": 0.9354838709677419,
        "is_first_child": false,
        "is_last_child": false
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It is requested that Grayson maintain documentation of the safety improvement costs associated with fulfilling this Compliance Order and submit the total to Gregory Ochs, Director, Central, Pipeline and Hazardous Materials Safety Administration. It is requested that these costs be reported in two categories: (1) total cost associated with preparation/revision of plans, procedures, studies and analyses, and (2) total cost associated with replacements, additions and other changes to pipeline infrastructure.",
      "text_span": "",
      "size": 9.0,
      "bold": 0,
      "font": "unknown",
      "all_cap": 0,
      "num_st": 0,
      "is_center": 0,
      "is_underline": 0,
      "label": "list_item",
      "page_no": 3,
